within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.L_AntineoplasticAndImmunomodulatingAgents.L01E_ProteinKinaseInhibitors.L01EB04_Osimertinib;
model Osimertinib "Osimertinib — default model: Osimertinib_Westra2025_reference"
  extends Osimertinib_Westra2025_reference;
  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>The default model of osimertinib: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.L_AntineoplasticAndImmunomodulatingAgents.L01E_ProteinKinaseInhibitors.L01EB04_Osimertinib.Osimertinib_Westra2025_reference\">Osimertinib_Westra2025_reference</a>, chosen among the models extracted from papers (reviewer verdict, ground-truth agreement, completeness). All models of osimertinib in this package:</p><ul><li><code>Osimertinib_Rodier2022_reference</code></li><li><code>Osimertinib_Westra2025_reference</code></li><li><code>Osimertinib_Jones2023_PD_tgi</code></li><li><code>Osimertinib_Jones2023_PD_pegfr</code></li></ul><h4>About osimertinib</h4><p>Osimertinib is a third-generation EGFR tyrosine kinase inhibitor used to treat non-small-cell lung cancer with a specific mutation. It is approved and authorised in the European Union for non-small-cell lung carcinoma.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q21506464\">Wikidata Q21506464</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Osimertinib\">Osimertinib</a>.</p></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from default: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: default</li></ul></body></html>"), experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 691200, Tolerance = 1e-9, Interval = 1));
end Osimertinib;
